  "major": "dance-ba-nyc-6f8ea5d3",
  "major_name": "Dance",
  "degree": "BA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Arts in Dance is an interdisciplinary program dedicated to dance studies in dialogue with or congruent to concert dance. This program offers a rigorous approach to the physical and verbal command of dance vocabulary, requiring the student to formulate aesthetic insights and apply them in the contexts of individual works, stylistic traditions, and historical and cultural awareness. The program emphasizes the importance of dance education as applied to pedagogical systems, theorizations of performance practices, an analysis of movement and its implications in a variety of arenas, and the emerging relationships between dance and media. BA candidates are given a solid foundation in dance technique and a balanced approach to coursework to facilitate the three concentrations in body, science, and motion; dance and media; and teaching dance arts. The curriculum is comprehensive, forward thinking, and pragmatic in its approach to future studies and careers in dance-related fields. It is nonperformance based and has the flexibility to meet the needs of dance students, dance professionals seeking a degree, and those interested in pursuing a double major in a related field.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nBA Language Requirements\nAll BA students are required to complete the BA degree language requirements, for a total of 12 semester hours of language study or demonstrated equivalent proficiency, as described in\nAdditional Requirements for BA students\n. Successful demonstration of proficiency does not reduce total minimum semester hours of study required to earn the BA degree.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nMajor Required Courses\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nBallet Course by Placement\nDANC 1450\nBallet 1\n4\nor\nDANC 2200\nBallet 2\nor\nDANC 2550\nBallet 3\nor\nDANC 3430\nBallet 4\nor\nDANC 4450\nBallet 5\nModern Course by Placement\nDANC 1890\nModern Dance 1\n4\nor\nDANC 2430\nModern Dance 2\nor\nDANC 3410\nModern Dance 3\nJazz Course by Placement\nDANC 1490\nJazz 1\n4\nor\nDANC 2490\nJazz 2\nor\nDANC 3490\nJazz 3\nAdditional Requirements\nDANC 1200\nStagecraft for Dance\n2\nDANC 2030\nRhythm in Sound and Movement\n2\nDANC 2220\nEmbodied Africanist Aesthetics\n4\nDANC 3540\nDance and Cultural Histories\n4\nDANC 3640\nCritical Approaches to Dance\n4\nDANC 4950\nSenior Seminar\n4\nLanguage Requirement\n12\nConcentrations\nComplete one of the following:\nBody, Science, and Motion\nDance and Media\nTeaching Dance Arts\nGeneral Electives/NUpath\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete any remaining semester hours after major to fulfill NUpath courses and to reach the minimum semester-hour program requirement.\nDance\nMajor Credit Requirement\nComplete 68 semester hours in the major.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required\nBody, Science, and Motion\nConcentration\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nBIOL 2217\nand\nBIOL 2218\nIntegrated Anatomy and Physiology 1\nand Lab for BIOL 2217\n5\nBIOL 2219\nand\nBIOL 2220\nIntegrated Anatomy and Physiology 2\nand Lab for BIOL 2219\n5\nDANC 2610\nIntroduction to Movement Analysis and Notation\n4\nDANC 3710\nSomatic Awareness\n4\nHSCI 1105\nHuman Nutrition\n4\nTHTR 4992\nDirected Study\n2\nDance and Media\nConcentration\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nCOMM 1122\nStorytelling Across Media\n4\nCOMM 2160\nDigital Sound Workshop\n4\nDANC 3510\nDance Composition 1\n4\nDANC 3700\nMovement, Media, and Theory\n4\nWith the assistance of an advisor, complete two courses from one of the following areas (both courses must be from the same subject code):\n8\nAudio Design and Production\nCOMM or MUST\nDigital Imaging and Web-Based Media\nARTF or ARTD\nGraphic Design\nARTG\nPhotography\nARTD\nVideo Production\nCOMM\nTeaching Dance Arts Concentration\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nDANC 2910\nMusic for Dance\n4\nDANC 3030\nExperiential Anatomy\n4\nDANC 3510\nDance Composition 1\n4\nDANC 3570\nTechniques for Teaching Dance 1\n4\nDANC 3710\nSomatic Awareness\n4\nDANC 4570\nTechniques for Teaching Dance 2\n4",
